# C's sql_alert_transitions() for a window (the SQL half of /api/v2/alert_transitions): the entries of the hosts
# listed that changed from or to WARNING or CRITICAL, with a global id inside the two ends, newest first. The rows
# are another hand's (`sql`): three hosts, seven alarms, two rules and an alarm whose rule has no row of
# alert_hash. Told apart by the steps: a host outside the list; the order of the list; the status boundary (both
# statuses exactly 2, one above, both below); the two ends to the microsecond (`before` is its second's first
# microsecond); three entries with one global id (C hands them out last stored first: the statement walks the
# index on the global id backwards); a global id of 0 with both ends 0; the context and the alert's name
# compared whole and with their case; ends the wrong way round; ends that wrap as C multiplies them; an alarm
# moved to another rule.
database real
